[38;5;231m⏺[39m I added a checkbox labelled "Mark as done" inside [38;5;153m<main>[39m in [38;5;153mindex.html[39m:

  [90m<[34mlabel[90m>[39m
    [90m<[34minput[90m [36mtype[90m=[31m"checkbox"[90m [36mid[90m=[31m"task-done"[90m>[39m
    Mark as done
  [90m</[34mlabel[90m>[39m

  It's a plain HTML checkbox, so the browser handles the on/off state. Wrapping it in a [38;5;153m<label>[39m means clicking the text
  toggles it too, and screen readers announce the label. There's no JavaScript or styling.

  Two things it doesn't do yet. The state isn't saved, so it resets when the page reloads. And there's only one
  checkbox, because the page doesn't have a task list yet. I can add saving with [38;5;153mlocalStorage[39m or one checkbox per task
  item if you want either.

